# Out past the village: the old shore, the forest, the southern hills and the
# bandit camp. See sim/dialogue/sim_dialogue.gd for the format.

=== smuggler
{self.suspicious} Smuggler: Close enough. That's close enough.
{quest.smuggler.done} Smuggler: Tide's turning. So am I.
{quest.smuggler.done} -> END
~ smuggler_known = 1
{package_taken} Smuggler: The Lantern. Marta. Before it starts to leak.
{package_taken} -> END
Smuggler: Nobody comes down to this beach. Nobody honest, anyway. Which are you?
* [Who's asking?] -> smuggler_job
* {talker.thievery >= 1} [(Thievery) Whatever's in those crates, we're not the law.] -> smuggler_job
* [We'll leave you to it.] -> END

=== smuggler_job
Smuggler: Somebody who needs a package carried to the village. The tavern. Quietly.
Smuggler: The guard knows my face. Yours, he doesn't. Marta pays on delivery.
* [Give it here.] -> smuggler_give
* [What's in it?] -> smuggler_contents
* [Not a chance.] -> END

=== smuggler_contents
Smuggler: Wine. Mostly. Does it matter?
-> smuggler_job

=== smuggler_give
{self.has.Sealed_package} ~ give Sealed package
~ package_taken = 1
Smuggler: Don't open it. Don't drop it. Don't get caught with it.
-> END

=== hermit
{self.suspicious} Wenna: The forest saw what you did. So did I.
{not hermit_met} Wenna: Visitors. The trees told me, but I didn't believe them.
{hermit_met} Wenna: Back again. The kettle's cold, but the books are dry.
~ hermit_met = 1
* [Who are you?] -> hermit_who
* [You have books?] -> hermit_books
* {talker.historian >= 1 and not hermit_lore} [(Historian) That mine in the north. What was it?] -> hermit_lore
* [Goodbye.] -> END

=== hermit_who
Wenna: A woman who prefers trees to people. The trees don't steal.
-> hermit

=== hermit_books
Wenna: Old learning. Fire, water, things that grow, things that rot. None of it free.
~ trade
-> END

=== hermit_lore
~ hermit_lore = 1
Wenna: Silver, once. The miners left in a hurry when the roof came down, and left things behind.
Wenna: The foreman hid his satchel up high, where thieves wouldn't look. Thieves never look up.
Wenna: And the side gallery they sealed with timbers. They said it was flooded. It wasn't.
-> END

=== shepherd
{quest.shepherd.rescued and not hob_thanked} -> shepherd_thanks
{quest.shepherd.rescued} Hob: My sheep found their own way home, they tell me. Clever beasts. Cleverer than me.
{quest.shepherd.rescued} -> END
Hob: Shh! They're right there! They'll hear you!
-> END

=== shepherd_thanks
~ hob_thanked = 1
~ shepherd_known = 1
Hob: You came for me? For an old shepherd? Gods. Here, take this. It was my wife's. She'd want it used.
{self.has.Amber_pendant} ~ give Amber pendant
Hob: I'll walk down to the village slowly. Very slowly.
-> END

=== prisoner
{joss_freed} Joss: Go on. I'll keep my head down till it's over.
{joss_freed} -> END
Joss: Psst. You're not one of them. Cut me loose, would you? Please?
* [Who are you?] -> prisoner_who
* [Hold still.] -> prisoner_free
* [Later.] -> END

=== prisoner_who
Joss: Joss. I drove the salt cart, before these louts took it. They keep me to haul and fetch.
-> prisoner

=== prisoner_free
~ joss_freed = 1
Joss: Bless you. Listen: the chief keeps lamp oil by the fire, right next to where he sleeps. One spark.
Joss: And the lookout on the tower can't see straight down behind it. Come round the back.
{self.has.Oil_flask} ~ give Oil flask
{self.has.Oil_flask} ~ give Oil flask
Joss: I stole those for the road. Use them better than I would.
-> END
